  "summary_en": "Binding Malaysian CAAM directive (Issue 01/Rev 01, 15 Nov 2022) setting standards and a certification process for agricultural drone operations, including Aerial Work Certificates, operator management systems, airworthiness, registration, remote pilot competency, pesticide dispensing rules, insurance, and audits.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "No agricultural UAS activity without a valid CAAM Aerial Work Certificate (private or commercial).",
   "Operations limited to VLOS/EVLOS, below 400 ft AGL, 50 m from uninvolved persons, Class G airspace; autonomous operations not allowed.",
   "Operators must maintain third-party liability insurance, an SMS, and nominated post holders.",
   "Remote pilots need RCoC; dispensing only DOA-listed payloads and registered pesticides.",
   "UAS registration marking, maintenance by authorised personnel, audits, and enforcement under Civil Aviation Act s24O."
